</div>
  <p>Similar to the [](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/File:Wikipedia-16px.png)&amp;#8201;<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverse_trigonometric_functions" target="_blank">arctangent</a>(<b>y</b>/<b>x</b>) except it utilizes the signs of <b>x</b> &amp; <b>y</b> to determine the quadrant and avoids division by zero.</p>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>If <b>x</b> is positive zero and...</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>y</b> is zero, <b>zero</b> is returned.</li>
    <li><b>y</b> is positive, <b>PI/2</b> is returned.</li>
    <li><b>y</b> is negative, <b>-PI/2</b> is returned.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If <b>x</b> is negative zero and...</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>y</b> is positive zero, <b>PI</b> is returned.</li>
    <li><b>y</b> is negative zero, <b>-PI</b> is returned.</li>
    <li><b>y</b> is positive, <b>PI/2</b> is returned.</li>
    <li><b>y</b> is negative, <b>-PI/2</b> is returned.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Or</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`if((string)x != (string)0.0 && y == 0.0)//negative zero
    return PI * ~-2*((string)y != (string)0.0));
return ((y > 0) - (y < 0)) * PI_BY_TWO;`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>The returned value is in the range <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PI" target="_blank">-[PI</a>, PI][[1]](#footnote_1).</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    local num1 = ll.Frand(100.0)
    local num2 = ll.Frand(100.0)

    ll.OwnerSay("y = " .. tostring(num1))
    ll.OwnerSay("x = " .. tostring(num2))

    ll.OwnerSay("The arctangent of y divided by x is " .. tostring(ll.Atan2(num1, num2)))
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
  state_entry()
  {
    float num1 = llFrand(100.0);
    float num2 = llFrand(100.0);

    llOwnerSay("y = " + (string)num1);
    llOwnerSay("x = " + (string)num2);

    llOwnerSay("The arctangent of y divided by x is " + (string)llAtan2(num1, num2));
  }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

--Function with input of a vector determining the position of a target and returning
--a string with the literal compass-direction of that target towards your position
--by Ramana Sweetwater 2009/01, any use allowed license :-)
--corrected by Patrick Muggins

local function compass(target)
    local source = ll.GetPos()
    local DIRS = {"W", "NW", "N", "NE", "E", "SE", "S", "SW", "W"}
    local index = ll.Ceil(3.5 - (4 * ll.Atan2(target.y - source.y, target.x - source.x) / PI))
    return ll.List2String(DIRS, index)
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//Function with input of a vector determining the position of a target and returning
//a string with the literal compass-direction of that target towards your position
//by Ramana Sweetwater 2009/01, any use allowed license :-)
//corrected by Patrick Muggins

string compass (vector target) 
{
    vector source = llGetPos();
    list DIRS =["W","NW","N","NE","E","SE","S","SW","W"];
    integer index = llCeil(3.5 - (4 * llAtan2(target.y - source.y, target.x - source.x) / PI));
    return llList2String(DIRS, index);
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
